cope&quot; receives only half the bonus they ordinarily would, rounding down.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">*Weatherprone</td> <td colspan=\"3\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Do not function in poor weather.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23938,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23938-gideoncrawle","user":"GideonCrawle","date":". 02-28-2018, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23938-gideoncrawle","name":"GideonCrawle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:39:06-08:00","id":1190220,"title":"","content":"*claps vigorously* No idea how balanced or accurate this is, but it looks like a lot of good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T06:00:25-08:00","id":1190229,"title":"","content":"What Aquatosic said.<br /> Though I have to say, I love what you did with the Special Rules there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T09:49:25-08:00","id":1190694,"title":"","content":"In terms of balance, the pistols should be okay. The most powerful of them is less powerful than many of the options available in the Armory or elsewhere; the only real question for me is whether the biggest shotguns aren't a bit OP. 4 (9-again), although equivalent to the top-tier shotgun damage in nWoD, is slightly high for CoD. If anything, this is all slightly underpowered, which is fine, because that's what I'm going for. The difference between modern Hunters trying to take down a raging werewolf with a Desert Eagle opposed to a Pinkerton Special Agent (my campaign) carrying only a five-shot popgun that effectively can't be reloaded in combat leads to a scrappy, desperate feel that encourages strategizing over confrontation and makes the decision to engage in combat that much more frightening. So far my group has only successfully driven off a Beast of Bethlehem, and despite &quot;winning,&quot; it was a bloodbath.<br /> <br /> If anyone uses these, please please let me know what you find!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23938-gideoncrawle","name":"GideonCrawle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T13:38:58-08:00","id":1190772,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you're facing a raging bullet dodging werewolf with a firearm you've done fucked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T16:00:47-08:00","id":1190832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1190161-old-west-civil-war-firearms-for-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1190772#post1190772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if you're facing a raging bullet dodging werewolf with a firearm you've done fucked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you might <i>feel</i> better! ...or cockier, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23938-gideoncrawle","name":"GideonCrawle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T20:03:27-08:00","id":1190891,"title":"","content":"Nice list! If anything, I'd say some of the guns are under-powered. 2 damage for a .69 caliber musket? Should probably be at least a 3, they had some decent energy (though of course they dropped off fast &gt;_&gt;). 9 agains really arn't that powerful, especially with GMC attacking rules. Some dude throwing around 10 dice would average around 3.33 successes with 10 again, and 3.74 success with a 9 again. Ironically, it means that the guns with a 9 again are slightly more accurate under GMC rules than a modern gun would be. Since the damage from these guns is added instead of adding dice like in 1E, it doesn't work like a skill check where adding a dice only adds ~3/10 chance for a success. Its basically an automatic success that only lands if you hit the attack, so a +1 damage is worth ~3 dice assuming the attack would hit anyway.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest you shave off the 9agains, and probably kick the damage up/down instead. They don't really work great as a half-way point, and they act kinda funky with the new rules.<br /> <br /> ~Edit~<br /> For clarification, I don't mean &quot;more accurate&quot; as in &quot;you will miss less often&quot;, since you need a success for the status to take effect. But if you got in a good-old fashioned shooting competition, the guy with a 9 again would have the edge :P<br /> It adds: 0.04/0.08/0.12 etc. ~0.04*n damage, with n being the number of dice you are trowing around. Some guy with 10 dice will get ~.4 extra damage on average, 40% of the 1 damage you would get from just bumping it up. Works good as long as your characters are all expert gunslingers in good conditions, falls apart the less dice you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 03-01-2018, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T13:44:29-08:00","id":1191110,"title":"","content":"All those damages were originally one higher, as a matter of fact, but I felt somewhat conscious of the admonition to decrease damages by one from what they would have been in the Armory. Perhaps I'll put them back after more playtesting.<br /> <br /> I agree as to the 9-agains being much more useful for characters who are more expert, and otherwise not so helpful--I'd had that thought myself, and was okay with it, since it gave characters who cared more about firearms more Options and otherwise was just color.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23938-gideoncrawle","name":"GideonCrawle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T20:38:21-08:00","id":1347829,"title":"","content":"Thank you for this firearms list. I will go use in my game. I thought the strength stat to use the rifles is low so I increased one point and increased the damage by one point as well. What IP means? And BP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25799-flashreverso","name":"FlashReverso","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}